<DocsLayout title="CLI (appmctl)" activeNav="/cli">
  <h1>CLI — <code>appmctl</code></h1>
  <p>
    <code>appmctl</code> is a dependency-light command-line client for the App Manager API.
    It ships as a single Bash 3.2-compatible executable, which makes it usable on CI
    runners and in minimal build images without installing a language runtime or SDK.
  </p>
  <p>
    Every command in this guide is shown with output recorded from a running instance, so
    what you read is what the CLI prints. The CLI is pre-1.0 (<code>0.3.0</code>): pin a
    commit in reproducible pipelines and expect the surface to keep moving with API v1.
  </p>

  <h2>Start here</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/cli/installation">Installation</a> — installer, custom directories, pinning a commit</li>
    <li><a href="/cli/configuration">Configuration</a> — environment variables, global options, API key scopes</li>
    <li><a href="/cli/examples">Examples</a> — end-to-end CI recipes</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>A first command</h2>
  <p>
    With <code>APP_MANAGER_API_KEY</code> and <code>APP_MANAGER_TEAM</code> exported, every
    read command works immediately:
  </p>
  <CommandOutput command="appmctl apps list" capture="apps-list" />

